WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.010
We are going to look for the silence of zone C in relation to zone A on the diaphragmatic plane.

2
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:15.560
There is a point of silence in the room. At some point, I will guide you. We will start from neutral.

3
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:25.450
We will gradually allow the patient's neutral to develop. We will focus on the micro-crystalline field. We take up all the space. The film on aikido.

4
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.550
To have the most therapeutic action...

5
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:39.107
as effective as possible, I must achieve a neutral state. Then, it is important to be able to bring out this neutral in my patient. It is something that must mature. And for

6
00:00:39.107 --> 00:01:07.987
that, we need the meeting point. Once I have a meeting point, the person, in confidence, can gradually disengage, let go towards their neutral. Gradually, these two neutrals will begin to blend. Once these two neutrals blend, I have a space, a more visible emergence that can appear from what we call primary respiration. Primary respiration is not something that is only in the body, it is present everywhere, a bit like the breath of life. We will just put ourselves

7
00:01:07.987 --> 00:01:10.867
in the awareness of this amniotic cavity, this

8
00:01:11.095 --> 00:01:18.515
zone B, and at the same time, little by little, we will dissociate our attention to go to the diaphragmatic pillars.

9
00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:23.025
These are the most fixed points of my diaphragm, they are pillars.

10
00:01:28.063 --> 00:01:33.743
And we will see that ultimately, these are enormous support points, almost a silent point.

11
00:01:33.823 --> 00:01:38.853
And we will gradually, with a little patience, bring out the neutral in a broader way.

12
00:01:42.203 --> 00:01:49.723
That is to say, we will also use the crystalline silence, we will rather speak of the crystalline immobility of the room.

13
00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:56.603
There is a kind of... In zone C, there is a kind of immobility that we must see.

14
00:01:56.603 --> 00:02:00.673
We will let the body center itself in relation to this zone C.

15
00:02:00.673 --> 00:02:05.673
Even if it seems subtle, it will happen by itself on a fluid, electrical plane.

16
00:02:05.673 --> 00:02:15.353
And then we will gradually, in this practice, begin to merge this silence of the room, or this dynamic immobility of the room, with the dynamic immobility at

17
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.850
the level of the diaphragmatic pillars. While being aware...

18
00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:31.490
of the amniotic cavity and all the integration of my vitelline vesicle to form my venous system. In this practice, to totally surrender to primary respiration,

19
00:02:32.338 --> 00:02:42.178
to the present movement, to the tide, that is to say, to the therapeutic force, to the power, and gradually let's see what it can do. The "hueil", in

20
00:02:44.178 --> 00:02:47.938
non-action, meaning I don't induce, I trust.

21
00:02:48.406 --> 00:02:49.576
the osteopath

